course: dictionary
lesson: 1815
title: Clumsily and how it is used
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Clumsily is an adverb. It tells you how someone does an action. Clumsily comes from clumsy, which means awkward with your body. «The puppy clumsily knocked over the water bowl.» The puppy did not mean to. It moved in an awkward, careless way.
explain: Clumsily has a second meaning, about words and actions done without skill or tact. «He clumsily asked her why she was late, and the room went quiet.» Nobody fell over, but the question was awkward and could hurt someone. Tact means knowing how to say things kindly.
explain: Writers use clumsily too. A sentence that is «clumsily written» is hard to read because its words do not flow well. Try reading it aloud. If it bumps and stops, it may need smoothing out.
explain: Use context clues. Falling, dropping and tripping point to the first meaning. Awkward remarks, teasing and hurt feelings point to the second. Check your meaning by swapping in awkwardly. If the sentence still makes sense, you have it right.
fact: Clumsily is an adverb, so it describes how an action is done.
fact: «Clumsily» means in an awkward, careless way, so that you knock things over, drop things or move badly.
fact: «Clumsily» can also mean said or done without skill or tact, so that it sounds awkward or rude.
fact: «Roadrunners can fly, but only short and clumsily.» They have short rounded wings and strong legs, and they belong to the cuckoo family.
fact: «Some children who like someone show it clumsily, by teasing, tugging or hiding their things.»
exercise: «The puppy clumsily knocked over the water bowl.» What does clumsily mean here? | Very quietly and slowly | With great skill and care | Happily, wagging its tail | *In an awkward, careless way
exercise: «Some children show it clumsily, by teasing, tugging or hiding their things.» What does clumsily suggest? | Quickly and neatly | *Without tact, so it sounds awkward | With great skill and kindness | Very loudly and proudly
exercise: Mia says her essay sounds clumsily written. What should she do? | Make the words longer so it sounds clever | Add more capital letters to every line | *Smooth the sentences so they read well | Hide it from her teacher
test: «The roadrunner moved clumsily over the stones.» Which word tells how the roadrunner moved? | *clumsily | roadrunner | stones | over
test: Tom says clumsily means quickly and neatly. Is he right? | *No, it means awkward and careless | Yes, it means quick and neat | Yes, it means exactly the same as carefully
exam: «He clumsily asked her why she was late, and the room went quiet.» What does clumsily mean here? | In a loud and happy voice | *Without tact, in a way that sounds awkward or rude | Quickly, as if in a race | With great skill and kindness
